description: After each completed build step, immediately proceed to the next without acknowledgment
alwaysApply: true
---

# Continuous build progression (no acknowledgment pauses)

- When the user is in build mode (for example: "continue build", "keep building", "do it"), do not pause after completing a step.
- After each completed step, immediately start the next concrete build step in the same flow.
- Do not send acknowledgment-only messages (for example: "done", "ready for next", "want me to continue?") between steps.
- Use this loop until blocked by an external action you cannot perform: implement -> verify -> commit/push (when requested by user/project rules) -> continue.
- Only stop to ask the user if a required external/manual action is needed and cannot be done from this environment.
